caption.p:
From Pickrell (10) data, 10 randomly selected samples from individuals are divided into two groups of 5, forming an artificial ‘null’ scenario. (a), (b) and (c) show barplots of log-counts-per-million (CPMs) of three genes from the top 10 DE genes with one or two extremely large observations. Dashed lines represent group-wise average log-CPMs. (d) and (e) plot genewise biological coefficient of variation (BCV) against gene abundance (in log2 counts per million) for edgeR and DESeq. In panel (d), gray dots show unmoderated biological BCV estimates (\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
