}{}
\begin{equation*}
{\rm log}(\mu _{gi}) = {X} \beta _g + \log N_i,
\end{equation*}
\end{document}where X is the design matrix containing the covariates (e.g. experimental conditions, batch effects, etc.), βg is a vector of regression parameters (a subset of which are of interest for differential expression inference) and Ni is the (effective) library size for sample i.

